      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This perspective strongly prioritizes the immediate, concrete good of preventing serious, real-world harm like a major attack or a lost person. In this view, the in-the-moment benefit to life and well-being clearly outweighs an abstract right to absolute privacy in a high-risk environment like a busy station.\n\nThe opposing side, though, often argues that the *systemic* risk of biased policing, constant state monitoring, and the \"chilling effect\" on free behavior is a more dangerous and ultimate threat to a free society over the long term.",
